### Macro file for "TOFmeter.cc"
### @author Tsuguo Aramaki
### @date 2015 March 23
### Updated 2026-10 for the TOF-meter geometry (DetectorConstruction.cc)

# --- Output ---
# /OutputDirectory, default ./ (created if missing)
# /OutputFile, base name: <dir>/<file>.dat and/or <dir>/<file>.root
# /InputDirectory
# /InputFile
# /gun/seed, random seed (applied immediately); /random/setSeeds also works
# /OutputFormat 0 ASCII step file .dat (default), 1 ROOT event ntuple .root, 2 both
# /OutputType 0 for all, 1 for simple mode (parent process, process name = 0)
# /EventFilter 0 every event in the ntuple (default), 1 only events with energy in an
#              active volume or a primary stopped inside the setup, 2 only events with
#              energy in a TOF bar or a Compton-detector layer (live time unaffected)
# /TrackType: 0 for all, 1 for trackID = 1, 2 for parentID = 1 only   (ASCII only)
# /TrackEdep: 0 for all, 1 for eDep > 0.0 keV                         (ASCII only)

# --- Primary generator ---
# /GeneralParticleSource 0 particle gun (/gun/...), 1 GPS (/gps/...), 2 cosmic rays (/tof/cosmic/...)
# /tof/cosmic/model expacs|guan        expacs: table of all species (default); guan: muon formula
# /tof/cosmic/expacsFile path          default data/expacs_spectrum.txt (scripts/expacs_to_table.py)
# /tof/cosmic/species all | names      expacs: e.g. mu+ mu- neutron proton e- e+ gamma alpha C12
#                                      (default mu+ mu-)
# /tof/cosmic/angular pairs            expacs: <species|all> <n|guan>, I ~ cos^n(theta); guan = muon
#                                      shape of Guan et al. (default all 2 mu+ guan mu- guan)
# /tof/cosmic/planeCenter x y z unit   centre of the horizontal source plane (default 0 0 75 cm)
# /tof/cosmic/halfX, halfY value unit  plane half sizes (default 150 cm)
# /tof/cosmic/energyMin, energyMax     kinetic energy range, per nucleon for ions (default 0 - 1000 GeV)
# /tof/cosmic/monoEnergy value unit    > 0: every particle gets this energy, zenith law of that
#                                      energy; flux and live time still from energyMin - energyMax
#                                      (the band it stands for); 0 = spectrum (default)
# /tof/cosmic/thetaMax value unit      maximum zenith angle (default 75 deg)
# /tof/cosmic/charge both|mu-|mu+      guan: muons to generate (default both)
# /tof/cosmic/chargeRatio 1.27         guan: mu+/mu-
#   The run prints the spectrum conditions, the flux through the plane and the live time.
# /physics_engine/neutron/timeLimit 10 ms   let slow neutrons live long enough to arrive

# --- Geometry (apply with /update) ---
# /tof/det/stations | frame | stack | absorber | leadWalls  true|false   parts of DetectorConstruction.cc
# /tof/det/leadThickness 10 cm         lead layer on the steel plate (bottom fixed, 0 = none);
#                                      the lead walls end level with its top
# /tof/det/print                       table of every placed volume (centre, size, z range)
# /tof/det/camera true|false                                 three-layer Compton camera
# /tof/det/worldMaterial G4_AIR                              (G4_Galactic for vacuum)
# /tof/det/worldSize 400 400 300 cm
# /tof/camera/position x y z unit     centre of CH2 (entrance layer)
# /tof/camera/rotateX angle unit      0 = looking up, 90 deg = looking towards -y
# /tof/camera/spacing21, spacing10    CH2-CH1 / CH1-CH0 centre-to-centre (25 / 35 mm)
# /tof/target/enable, material, size, position      target box (未知材料)
# /tof/degrader/enable, material, size, position    degrader box (降速铅砖)
# /tof/blocks/add name material x y z dx dy dz unit  passive box, e.g. lead brick (centre, full sizes)
# /tof/blocks/clear
# /CheckOverlap: 0 for off, 1 for on (default on)
# /update: rebuild the geometry now; needed whenever geometry is changed

# /tof/vis/spin 10                    Qt GUI only: turn the viewer at 10 deg/s until the first
#                                      click, scroll or key press in it; 0 stops
# /Visualization default 0 (unused by DetectorConstruction.cc)

# set active sensitive detector
# /hits/inactivate DetectorSD
# /process/inactivate muMinusCaptureAtRest
# /particle/process/list: show the list of physics processes
